# Design check as a flow diagram

A diagram can sit beside the numbers it describes. The fence below is drawn from its text, so
editing the steps redraws it. The calculation under it follows the same steps.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  A[Loads: w and span L] --> B[Design moment M*]
  B --> C[Section capacity phi Ms]
  C --> D{M* <= phi Ms?}
  D -- yes --> E[Section passes]
  D -- no --> F[Increase the section]
  F --> C
```

## Inputs
L: 6 m | span
w: 12 kN/m | design uniform load
fy: 300 MPa | yield strength
Ze: 1.23e6 mm³ | effective section modulus
phi: 0.9 | capacity factor

## Steps
Mstar: w * L^2 / 8 -> kN*m | design moment
phiMs: phi * fy * Ze -> kN*m | design capacity
utilisation: Mstar / phiMs -> % | ratio of action to capacity

if utilisation <= 100 %: "OK: the section passes." else: "Fails: increase the section."
